+# UI9 hand-back — 2026-10-06
+
+UI9 refines the 340-point menu popover with layered link cards, compact pill actions, and a quieter footer. It moves the dark surface from near-black to graphite gray, with a subtle remote burgundy haze, and changes the menu mark's edge to a theme-aware neutral gray while preserving the signed B/I.A pixels. Longer engine status lines wrap without an artificial cutoff.
+
+Baseline was 379 engine / 94 app tests. Final is **379 engine / 95 app tests (77 BatonUI + 18 BatonKit)**; `swift build` passes. The fixture bundle was refreshed and relaunched with its saved Dark selection. Native window inspection shows the gray palette; ImageRenderer snapshots show the compact popover and both menu-outline appearances. The system menu-bar popover itself was not directly captured.
+
+## Exact paths
+
+- `app/Sources/BatonUI/Theme/Theme.swift`
+- `app/Sources/BatonUI/Components/BrandMark.swift`
+- `app/Sources/BatonUI/Screens/Popover/PopoverView.swift`
+- `app/Tests/BatonUITests/BrandTests.swift`
+- `app/Tests/BatonUITests/PopoverTests.swift`
+- `docs/plan/STATUS.md`
+- `docs/plan/track-d-app.md`
+- `docs/plan/reports/UI9-2026-10-06.md`
+
+## Challenge and independent review
+
+Root's challenge found that the first ImageRenderer attempt omitted SwiftUI's native scrolling subtree and produced a footer-only image. The compact preview now uses the existing snapshot-presentation path, and the inspected PNG contains the link card, Continue actions, recent-chat action, and footer. Content is still engine-provided; no static user-facing copy was introduced.
